camlab-rpi (1.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release. Notes:
    https://github.com/Kurokesu/camlab-rpi/releases/tag/v1.0.1
  * Floor rpicam-apps-core at 1:1.12.0+krks1. A bare name was satisfied
    by the Raspberry Pi build images ship.

 -- Danius Kalvaitis <danius@kurokesu.com>  Mon, 11 Aug 2026 10:35:00 +0300

camlab-rpi (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release. Notes:
    https://github.com/Kurokesu/camlab-rpi/releases/tag/v1.0.0
  * Rename source and binary package to camlab-rpi. Suite names an OS
    release and architecture names a CPU, neither names a board, so a
    port to another arm64 board has nowhere to go.
  * Install /usr/bin/camlab-setup, symlinked to install.sh in the
    payload.
  * Move sensor drivers from Depends to Suggests. camlab-setup installs
    them after kernel pruning.

 -- Danius Kalvaitis <danius@kurokesu.com>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 19:40:00 +0300

camlab (1.0.0~beta.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release. Notes:
    https://github.com/Kurokesu/camlab-rpi/releases/tag/v1.0.0-beta.4
  * Add wlr-randr, camlab uses it to settle HDMI against a DSI touch
    panel before the window opens.

